    },
    "body": "The same mixture as the previous round - the 1,100-document short-premise store with 9,360 response tokens - at 33,773,500 parameters against 19,929,136. Form compliance holds and content is still ungrounded, but retention is still not answered and still in the store own register: Noted. and I see., turn-1 acknowledgements from the store family, where 19.9M returned Noted. and Noted. So 1.7x parameters changed the variant and not the failure. Binding is not a capacity problem in this range, which rules out the last more-of-the-same remedy. Form compliance and binding have different causes and only one is data: compliance was bought by data shape and survives four configurations, two shapes, two weights and a 70 percent smaller store; binding has survived three data designs and a capacity increase, leaving the objective and the architecture. Four failed routes documented; the remaining work is a mechanism or objective change. References #820",
